{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.allOdd_compIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.allOdd_compIdx","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L197-L202","doc":"…and with all runs odd (`e ≡ 1`) every strand is in ONE component — the other\nextreme, showing `compIdx` is not constant-by-construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.allEven_compIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.allEven_compIdx","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L189-L195","doc":"**Not vacuous** — the carrier's own shape. All runs even (`e ≡ 2`): every generator\nopens a component, so `compIdx i = i` and the components are the singletons, linked in a\npath. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.linking_only_between_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.linking_only_between_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L174-L187","doc":"**The path linking graph, derived.** Components can only be linked when they are\nadjacent: a nonzero linking number between components `c` and `d` comes from some run\nwhose two strands lie in `c` and `d`, and by `components_differ_iff_even` such a run\nputs them at `compIdx g` and `compIdx g + 1`.\n\n`PathCarrier` in `OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean` takes this as a\nhypothesis, and the whole arc has carried the `P_μ` shape as a measurement. Stated here\nin the form the argument delivers: the only pairs a run can link are consecutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.distinct_even_generators_distinct_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.distinct_even_generators_distinct_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L162-L172","doc":"**Tier 1, one generator per component pair.** Two different even runs open two\ndifferent component boundaries — so a pair of components crosses at exactly one\ngenerator, and in particular the two generators of a chain triple differ.\n\nThe proof is that `compIdx` is monotone and jumps at every even run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_lt_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_lt_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L157-L160","doc":"An even run strictly advances the component index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_mono","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L143-L155","doc":"Component index never decreases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.even_of_components_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.even_of_components_differ","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L136-L141","doc":"**Tier 1, even run length.** A run that crosses two distinct components has even\nexponent — so the `2m` of `underSum_eq_linking` is not an observation about the sampled\nwords but a property of every inter-component run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.components_differ_iff_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.components_differ_iff_even","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L125-L134","doc":"**The result, and it is the whole file.** The two strands crossing in run `g` lie in\ndifferent components exactly when `e g` is even — and when they do, the components are\n**adjacent**, `compIdx g` and `compIdx g + 1`.\n\nEverything tier 1 asserts is a reading of this one statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_pStart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_pStart","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L110-L123","doc":"Along an odd run nothing changes component: the left strand of run `g` is in the\nsame component as position `g` itself.\n\nThis is the step that makes the file work — it says `pStart` never escapes its\ncomponent, so the pair crossing at run `g` is `(something in component compIdx g,\nstrand g+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_succ","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L106-L108","doc":"Crossing into the next strand costs a component exactly at an even run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.compIdx","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L94-L102","doc":"Which component of the closure strand `i` belongs to: the number of even-exponent\ngenerators strictly below it.\n\nOdd runs fuse consecutive strands into one cycle; an even run is where one component\nends and the next begins. Written as a count rather than as a cycle decomposition\nbecause that is the only property anything below needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.pStart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure.pStart","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordComponentStructure.lean#L85-L92","doc":"The strand sitting at position `g` when run `R_g` begins.\n\n`pStart e 0 = 0` (nothing has moved yet). After run `g`: if `e g` is even the pair is\nrestored, so position `g+1` holds strand `g+1` and the next run's left strand is `g+1`;\nif `e g` is odd they are swapped, so the left strand is carried over unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}